<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Assore yr shr surges, div climbs.</title>
<headline>Assore yr shr surges, div climbs.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     4,230	 vs 1,900</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		   700	 vs   550</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   59.21	 vs 26.60</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   35.14	 vs 32.15</p>
<p>    Tax			 10.07	 vs  5.69</p>
<p>    Turnover		  22.59	 vs 19.80</p>
<p>Div payable Nov 8</p>
<p>on register Oct 18</p>
<p>Full name: The Associated Ore and Metal Corp Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that prices of manganese were unlikely to change significantly in the current financial year, while iron ore prices should show some improvement. Sales volumes for maganese and iron ore were not expected to change substantially. It said the ferromanganese market was expected to remain firm, while demand and prices for ferrochrome were not expected to improve significantly.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
